106	Integrable -> content on the ring of sets generated by predictable rectangles.
107	Can be extended to a measure on the predictable $\sigma$-algebra if the process is of class DL and ... (see Metivier, Semimartingales, 13.3).
108	
109	Let $X : T \to \Omega \to E$ be a stochastic process such that $X_t$ is integrable for all $t$~.
110	For $s < t$ and $A \in \mathcal{F}_s$, let
111	\begin{align*}
112	  \mu_X((s, t] \times A) = \mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_A (X_t - X_s)]
113	  \: .
114	\end{align*}
115	Set $\mu_X(\{0\} \times A) = 0$~.
116	Then $\mu_X$ is a content on the predictable rectangles, which can be extended to the ring of sets it generates.
